<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mercedarians</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1218</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Order of Our Lady of Mercy</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Mercedarians, the Order of Our Lady of Mercy, are a Catholic religious order founded in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barcelona">Barcelona</a> about 1218 by Peter Nolasco to ransom Christians held captive by Muslims. Their members took a special vow to offer themselves as hostages if needed to free captives. For six centuries they raised funds in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> and elsewhere and redeemed thousands of captives from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-africa">North Africa</a>, especially <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algiers">Algiers</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mercedarians.jpg" alt="Mercedarians" width="320" height="421" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Vicente López Portaña · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Virgin_of_Mercy.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
